  "assumptions": [
    "This is a fully synthetic deterministic 720-hour service schedule; it is not a measured fleet, weather history, reliability estimate or field availability claim.",
    "Three equivalent active HAPS service-capacity units are required throughout the 30-day illustrative service window.",
    "HAPS-A, HAPS-B and HAPS-C are the three primary units. HAPS-D is one ground-ready spare that contributes zero service while in ground_ready, launching, recovering or undergoing maintenance.",
    "HAPS-A has one planned 24-hour maintenance window at hours 240–264; HAPS-B has one planned 24-hour maintenance window at hours 480–504; the windows do not overlap.",
    "HAPS-C has one 24-hour synthetic unscheduled repair from hours 360–384.",
    "Reserve launch lead time is 12 hours. The scheduled maintenance replacements are launched in advance; after the HAPS-C fault, the first 12 hours are unserved before HAPS-D reaches station.",
    "The reserve remains on station for 24 hours for each maintenance/fault replacement cycle, then undergoes a declared 12-hour recovery and becomes ground-ready again.",
    "One common-cause weather event occurs from hours 600–624. Its 0.7 multiplier applies to every platform's service contribution, and launch/recovery sites are closed for this interval. The multiplier is a synthetic service derating, not a particular wind speed or validated flight limit.",
    "Capacity adequacy is capped at the full service requirement: extra HAPS capacity above three units does not earn extra availability credit.",
    "The no-spare baseline uses only HAPS-A, HAPS-B and HAPS-C with identical maintenance, repair and common-cause event timelines; the reserve HAPS-D contributes nothing because it is not in that fleet comparator.",
    "The exact oracle partitions the 720-hour window at every platform-state and common-cause event boundary and integrates effective service capacity; no stochastic or Monte Carlo estimates are used.",
    "This fixture does not model launch vehicle operations, weather forecasting, specific airworthiness procedures, human staffing levels, component supply chain, battery ageing, thermal coupling, radio capacity or legal permission.",
    "Aerial platform endurance, fleet availability, service capacity adequacy and common-cause resilience are distinct metrics and must not be interchanged."
